Little Colorado R near Cameron gauge has a gap of 731 days ending on 1994-12-31
Colorado R Below Hoover Dam gauge has a gap of 239 days ending on 2023-03-26

1.2 CONUS State Boundaries
Use tigris::states() to get US state boundaries, filter to CONUS, and transform to the equidistant projection.


Code
states &lt;- states(cb = TRUE, progress_bar = FALSE) |&gt;
  filter(!STUSPS %in% c("AK", "HI", "PR", "AS", "GU", "MP", "VI")) |&gt;
  st_transform(eqdc)

2.1 Distance to US National Border (km)
The national border is the resolved outer boundary of all states — internal state lines dissolved, only the coastline and land borders remain.
Store the result as a new column dist_to_border in your cities data frame. Produce a flextable of the 5 cities farthest from the national border — include city name, state, and distance.


Code
#functions
make_border_line &lt;- function(x, dissolve = TRUE) {if (dissolve) {x |&gt; 
    st_union() |&gt; 
    st_cast("MULTILINESTRING")} else {x |&gt; 
        st_combine() |&gt; 
        st_cast("MULTILINESTRING")}}


add_distance_km &lt;- function(cities, target_geom, col_name) {cities |&gt;
    mutate(!!col_name := st_distance(geometry, target_geom)[ ,1] |&gt;
        set_units("km") |&gt;
        drop_units())}


top_cities &lt;- function(data, sort_col, n = 5) {data |&gt;
    arrange(desc(.data[[sort_col]])) |&gt;
    slice_head(n = n)}




Code
national_border &lt;- make_border_line(states)

cities &lt;- add_distance_km(cities, national_border, "dist_to_border")

farthest_cities_nb &lt;- top_cities(cities, "dist_to_border") 




Code
ft_table_one &lt;- farthest_cities_nb |&gt;
    select(city, state_id, dist_to_border) |&gt;
    st_drop_geometry() |&gt;
    flextable() |&gt;
      set_header_labels(city = "City", state_id = "State", dist_to_border = "Distance (km)") |&gt;
  set_caption(paste0("U.S. Cities Farthest from the National Border")) |&gt;
  autofit()

